  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_abs_q7.c ****  * \par Conditions for optimum performance
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_abs_q7.c ****  *  Input and output buffers should be aligned by 32-bit
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_abs_q7.c ****  *
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_abs_q7.c ****  *
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_abs_q7.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_abs_q7.c ****  * \par
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_abs_q7.c ****  * The function uses saturating arithmetic.
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_abs_q7.c ****  * The Q7 value -1 (0x80) will be saturated to the maximum allowable positive value 0x7F.
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_abs_q7.c ****  */
